  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Myanmar Technical Officer WHO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The conflict in Myanmar continues to escalate, further exacerbating the already dire humanitarian situation in the country. Some 18.6 million people are estimated to require humanitarian assistance in 2024, one million more than the same time last year. This is almost 19 times the number prior to the military takeover and equivalent to a third of the population. The public healthcare system has collapsed and there is a lack of access to services, especially in conflict affected areas.Between 12 June and 18 July 2024, the country has witnessed a resurgence of acute water diarrhoea (AWD) and cholera outbreaks, with confirmed cases being reported both in conflictaffected areas and townships falling under the under the control of State Administration Council (SAC) and de facto health authorities.The incumbent will provide technical expertise in planning, monitoring, evaluating, coordinating, and implementing support on WASH activities, including provision of safe drinking water, adequate sanitation, hygiene, and infection control at the principal hospitals of the State of Yangon being used for patients referral and admission. The incumbent will also support coordination with the de facto authorities and other partners for safe and dignified burial of contagious bodies and medical waste management.</narrative>
  </description>
